@copilot Close the latest-dependency coverage gap in this PR while retaining the three regression scenarios: direct HttpResponseException without a cause must not report an error for HTTP 200; direct HttpResponseException with a real cause must report that cause on the direct-decorator path; a wrapped HttpResponseException must remain a failure.

In instrumentation/armeria/armeria-1.3/javaagent/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/armeria/v1_3/ArmeriaHttpServerTest.java, responseExceptionWithCauseIsReported currently skips all latest-dependency runs because its endpoint calls initCause(). Older Armeria permits initCause(), but newer Armeria initializes the cause in its constructor and supports HttpResponseException.of(HttpResponse, Throwable) instead. Make the attached-cause scenario run with both baseline and latest dependencies, using the smallest maintainable test setup compatible with baseline compilation. Do not merely delete the assumption while retaining the incompatible initCause() call.

Verify the real HTTP/2 library-fallback behavior separately on baseline and latest Armeria. The existing UNSET/no-exception expectation reflects old Armeria discarding response-control causes before the request log sees them; do not assume latest Armeria has the same limitation. Keep assertions accurate for the actual instrumentation path and dependency version, with useful attached-cause coverage on latest dependencies. Preserve the existing intended production classification and rethrow behavior, and avoid unrelated changes. Run the relevant HTTP/1 and HTTP/2 tests against baseline and latest dependencies, plus the existing Armeria 1.9 suite when affected. Apply the narrowest spotlessApply before validation. Update this existing PR rather than creating an unrelated PR.

